<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal's S.Costa H1 net drops sharply.</title>
<headline>Portugal's S.Costa H1 net drops sharply.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jan 1 to June 30:</p>
<p>(billion escudos, unless stated)</p>
<p>Cons net 0.184 vs 0.869</p>
<p>Operating result 1.49 vs 1.813</p>
<p>Financial result 1.339 loss vs 1.657 loss</p>
<p>Turnover 33.667 vs 49.871</p>
<p>Net assets 93.077 vs 94.057</p>
<p>Liabilities 69.241 vs 70.266</p>
<p>Note - Soares da Costa is a Portuguese construction company. &quot;Turnover in the first half was 33.7 billion escudos, of which 28.9 billion escudos (86 percent of the total) were generated by the parent company,&quot; Soares da Costa said in a statement. &quot;The drop by about one third, relative to turnover in the first half of 1995, was due to earnings from construction of Macau airport (in 1995), and the frequent interruptions and delays caused by bad weather in Portugal during most of the first half 1996.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Lisbon newsroom 351-1-3538254</p>
</text>
